# Project Style Guide

Follow `STYLE_GUIDE.md` for this project. These are guidelines, not rigid rules—prefer clarity and maintainability.

## Goals

- Explicit over implicit
- Readable and maintainable
- Consistent patterns across similar code
- Logic before presentation (prepare data, then render HTML)

## Key Preferences

| Do | Avoid |
|----|-------|
| `??` for simple default values | Ternary operators (`? :`) |
| Explicit `if` for conditional logic | Conditional assignment (`$x = condition === value`) |
| `switch` for multiple branches | Nested ternaries |
| Tabs for indentation | Spaces for indentation or column alignment |
| Pre-compute variables before HTML | Complex expressions inline in templates |
| Descriptive names (`$is_manual`, `$should_sync_excerpt`) | Abbreviated or opaque names (`$manual`, `$sync`) |

## Markup (HTML, CSS, JS)

- Do not add animations, transitions, drop shadows, or gradients unless specified
- Do not introduce new fonts, colors, borders, or border-radius—use project-provided UI tokens
- Keep vertical spacing consistent between sections and between paragraph-level items
- Prefer `px` for CSS sizing; use media queries when spacing changes by viewport

## Architecture

- **Boiler** (`includes/Admin/`, `includes/Core/`): generic partial CPT, content sync, backup/restore, classic editor, and theme shell. Must not import Example* classes.
- **Example product** (`includes/ExampleAdmin/`, `includes/ExampleCore/`, `includes/ExampleFront/`): sample site layer. Hooks into boiler via filters in `ExampleCore\BoilerIntegration` and `ExampleCore\ExampleThemeShell`.
- Example → boiler is OK (filters, `PartialStore`, `Core::get_instance()`). Boiler → Example is not.

When editing PHP, apply `.cursor/rules/php-style.mdc`. When editing HTML, CSS, or JS, apply `.cursor/rules/markup-style.mdc`.
